<div class="prose source-catalog"><p class="eyebrow">The collection behind the course</p><h1>Study the marks. Credit the source.</h1><p>All reference images are local derivatives of official museum downloads. Untouched originals and their checksums are retained in the project. Crops are converted to grayscale and their tonal range normalized for legibility; no crop is enlarged beyond its source resolution.</p><p>Selected images are public domain and available under the museums’ Open Access policies: <a href="https://www.metmuseum.org/policies/image-resources">The Met</a> and <a href="https://www.nga.gov/terms-and-notices">National Gallery of Art</a>. Instructional text is written for this course. Any construction guide is course analysis, not a reconstruction of an artist’s historical process.</p>
{% for ref in references %}<section><h2>{{ ref.artist }}</h2><figure class="reference-card"><a href="{{ (ref.overview.path) | url }}"><img src="{{ (ref.overview.path) | url }}" width="{{ ref.overview.width }}" height="{{ ref.overview.height }}" alt="Full reference sheet: {{ ref.title }}" loading="lazy"></a><figcaption><cite>{{ ref.title }}</cite>, {{ ref.date }}. {{ ref.medium }}.<span class="source">{{ ref.museum }} · {{ ref.rights }}<br><a href="{{ ref.objectUrl }}">{{ ref.objectUrl }}</a><br>Retrieved {{ ref.retrievedAt }} · Rights reviewed {{ ref.rightsReviewedAt or ref.retrievedAt }}</span></figcaption></figure></section>{% endfor %}</div>
